  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional sustainability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fundacin Integral Campesina in Costa Rica, $50,000 over two years; counterpart committed, $78,700 FINCA will design and test procedures and criteria for administering a fund that provides seed capital to community credit businesses (CCBs) owned by residents and grassroots associations. The CCBs makes loans to their members based on rules defined during a training process coordinated by FINCA, which will assess whether investing in the CCBs yields sufficient income to cover its institutional costs. The project should benefit 200 Costa Ricans.</narrative>
  </description>
